          "**Confidence intervals**: a 95% CI crossing **1 for ratios** (RR, OR, HR) or **0 for differences** (ARR, mean difference) is not significant; a wide interval means an imprecise, underpowered study. [Sundar Rao 5e]",
          "**Systematic review and meta-analysis**: explicit reproducible search (PRISMA 2020, PROSPERO registration), inverse-variance weighting; on a **forest plot** each line is a study's CI, the square's area is its weight, the vertical line is no effect and the **diamond is the pooled estimate** - significant if it does not touch the line. [Cochrane Handbook 6.4]",
          "**Heterogeneity**: I-squared 0-40% may not be important, 30-60% moderate, 50-90% substantial, 75-100% considerable; **publication bias** is looked for with a **funnel plot** (asymmetry suggests missing small negative trials). [Cochrane Handbook 6.4]",
