          "The classification that goes with it is the **flags system** - **red** (serious pathology), **yellow** (psychosocial risk of chronicity), **orange** (psychiatric disorder), **blue** (perceptions of work) and **black** (system and policy obstacles) - in the table below. [NICE NG59 2020]",
          "In Indian practice the **family is effectively a fourth axis** - decisions on surgery, insulin or admission are often made by the family, not the patient alone. [Park 28e]",
